--_000_4414AEBBCFB2B648B49E5766D309768E9807B25C2FMAIL_
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="us-ascii"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

All,

Attached is an animation that may help you visualize the Chlorine induced o=
xidative degradation failure mechanism of PE.  It shows the antioxidant mol=
ecules being used up and overwhelmed in their defense against the chlorine =
molecules.  Eventually the PE surface is undefended by antioxidant molecule=
s and exposed to chlorine attack resulting in degradation (meaning it is we=
akened).  When weakened a crack initiates on the pipe ID surface and then p=
ropagates to through wall failure in time.

You must use your imagination when viewing this model.  You are looking at =
a section of pipe wall thickness along the pipe longitudinal axis.  If you =
cannot open this file let me know.

Recall that elevated temperatures are required to cause this to happen.  Th=
is would be temperatures that will be present in the Sunbelt.

This is not ready to be deployed to customers.  Thank you John Fralick for =
suggesting this.

Again, the latest series of blurts is not meant for you to then take to cus=
tomers.  You should try to understand the "why" of these issues.  Hopefully=
 you see the commercial ramifications of them.  Ultimately we have to decid=
e what of this to take to the market.  In order for you to take this to the=
 market in whatever form we choose you first would preferably understand it=
 so that you can believe in it.  Belief is required for you to more effecti=
vely use whatever tools we deploy.  We rely on all of you to help identify =
those things that are useful and how they might be used.

J

